The worklist is five classes. The Rust side already contains source-linked implementations for the major server behaviors: dragon damage/phase/death handling, structure coordinate/fill/chest helpers, animal love/breeding hooks, attribute calculation/persistence, and pot interaction/wobble. I’m now checking the remaining real observability gaps, especially deferred decorated-pot loot and placement components, before deciding whether any patch is justified.
The five worklist entries are enumerated; the audit is focused on distinguishing existing Rust equivalents from real server-visible omissions, with deferred decorated-pot loot as the main unresolved candidate.
